course: dictionary
lesson: 8766
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to use. «The house was severely damaged» means the house was badly hurt. The word tells you how the damage happened.
explain: «He was severely punished» means he was punished strictly or harshly. «A severely plain dress» means a dress with no decoration at all. Ask yourself: is the sentence about how bad something is, how strict someone is, or how plain something looks?
explain: Check your choice by swapping the meaning into the sentence. «The road was severely flooded» means badly flooded, so it fits the danger in a news report about a severe weather warning.
fact: Severely is an adverb, so it tells you how something happens.
fact: «Severely» can mean very badly or seriously: «severely injured» means badly hurt.
fact: «Severely» can mean strictly or harshly: «severely punished» means punished strictly.
fact: «Severely» can mean plainly, without decoration: «a severely plain dress».
fact: In maths, «sales fell severely» means sales dropped a lot.
exercise: «The house was severely damaged by the storm.» What does severely mean here? | Without any decoration | *Very badly | Quietly | Strictly, with rules
exercise: «In the story, the strict teacher spoke severely to the noisy class.» What does severely mean here? | *Strictly or harshly | Happily | Very badly | Plainly, with no decoration
exercise: «The dress was severely plain, with no bows or lace.» What does severely mean here? | Very quickly | *Plainly, without decoration | Very badly | Harshly
test: «The cyclist was severely injured in the crash.» What does severely mean here? | Quietly | *Very badly or seriously | Strictly, with rules | Plainly, without decoration
test: «Sales fell severely in the winter.» What does severely show? | No change at all | A rise in sales | *A big, serious drop | Only a small drop
exam: «The park's rules were severely limited after the flood.» What does severely mean here? | Quickly | Happily | *Very badly or seriously | Plainly, without decoration
